  "notes": "{市販薬|しはんやく} (also called OTC{医薬品|いやくひん}) is available at drugstores and pharmacies without a prescription. In Japan, they are classified into categories with different sales restrictions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {市販薬|しはんやく}を{買|か}う (to buy OTC medicine)\n- {市販薬|しはんやく}で{治|なお}す (to cure with OTC medicine)\n- {市販薬|しはんやく}の{風邪薬|かぜぐすり} (OTC cold medicine)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {処方薬|しょほうやく}: prescription medicine\n- ドラッグストア: drugstore\n- {薬局|やっきょく}: pharmacy\n- {第一類|だいいちるい}{医薬品|いやくひん}: first-class OTC drugs (pharmacist consultation required)",
